<h2 id="ascii" style="color:#1565c0;font-size:1.22em;font-weight:650;border-left:4px solid #42a5f5;padding-left:10px;margin-top:1.1em">2. ASCII wireframe conventions</h2>

<h3 id="ascii-frame" style="color:#00695c;font-size:1.05em;font-weight:600;margin-top:0.85em">2.1 Outer frame</h3>

Use **box-drawing** characters for the viewport (`┌─┐│└┘├┤`). Fence with language tag **`text`**.

```text
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│  {App / product title}                                                       │
├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│  {Global nav / primary chrome}                                               │
├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│  {Secondary nav or context bar — omit if N/A}                                │
├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│  {Page body — tabs, filters, main content}                                   │
│                                                                              │
├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│  {Footer / session / actions — omit if N/A}                                  │
└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

Adapt band count to the app (2–5 bands). **Name each band** in annotations (see §2.2).

<h3 id="ascii-symbols" style="color:#00695c;font-size:1.05em;font-weight:600;margin-top:0.85em">2.2 Symbols</h3>

| Symbol | Meaning |
|---|---|
| `●` | Active / selected item in that row |
| `[ Label ]` | Button, link, or nav item |
| `( Label )` | Chip, tag, or filter pill |
| `▾` | Dropdown trigger |
| `…` | Truncated items |
| `← callout` | Right-margin annotation (same line or line below) |
| `(hold)` | Planned but not shipped |

<h3 id="ascii-annotations" style="color:#00695c;font-size:1.05em;font-weight:600;margin-top:0.85em">2.3 Annotations</h3>

Add short `←` callouts per band:

```text
│  [ Home ]  [ Settings ● ]  [ Help ]              ← primary nav
│  Tab A ● │ Tab B │ Tab C                         ← section tabs
│  (filter 1)  (filter 2 ●)                        ← in-page filters
```

Long rationale stays in prose **below** the fence, not inside the box.

---

<h2 id="in-page" style="color:#1565c0;font-size:1.22em;font-weight:650;border-left:4px solid #42a5f5;padding-left:10px;margin-top:1.1em">3. In-page hierarchy</h2>

Show **named** levels — never an unnamed blob of content:

```text
│  TABS:   [ Overview ● ]  [ Details ]  [ History ]
│  CHIPS:  ( All )  ( Active ● )  ( Archived )
│  CONTENT: table / form / cards for active selection
│  ACTIONS: [ Save ]  [ Cancel ]
```

Guidelines:

1. **Prefer 3–4 tabs** per page; deeper topics → chips inside one tab.
2. Label controls with **user-facing names**, not component or DB identifiers.
3. Mark **empty, loading, error** states in a separate mini-wireframe when behavior matters.

