<h2 id="mermaid" style="color:#1565c0;font-size:1.22em;font-weight:650;border-left:4px solid #42a5f5;padding-left:10px;margin-top:1.1em">4. Mermaid for UI-related diagrams</h2>

<h3 id="mermaid-types" style="color:#00695c;font-size:1.05em;font-weight:600;margin-top:0.85em">4.1 Diagram types</h3>

| Goal | Mermaid type | Example |
|---|---|---|
| Site / IA tree | `graph TD` | App → areas → pages |
| User click path | `graph LR` or `graph TD` | List → detail → edit |
| Conditional UI | `{Decision}` diamond | Role gate · feature flag |
| Teaching / prerequisite order | `graph TD` | Step A before step B |

<h3 id="mermaid-style" style="color:#00695c;font-size:1.05em;font-weight:600;margin-top:0.85em">4.2 Style (readable in docs)</h3>

- **5–11 nodes** per diagram; split if larger.
- Break long labels with `\n` inside nodes.
- Optional semantic colors on `style` lines:

```mermaid
graph TD
  A[Entry / trigger] --> B{Decision}
  B --> C[Primary screen]
  B --> D[Alternate screen]

  style A fill:#e3f2fd,stroke:#1976d2,stroke-width:1px,font-size:9px
  style B fill:#fff8e1,stroke:#ff8f00,stroke-width:1px,font-size:9px
  style C fill:#e8f5e9,stroke:#2e7d32,stroke-width:1px,font-size:9px
  style D fill:#ede7f6,stroke:#5e35b1,stroke-width:1px,font-size:9px
```

- **Blue:** entry / sources · **Amber:** decisions · **Green:** target screens · **Purple:** secondary paths

<h3 id="mermaid-vs-ascii" style="color:#00695c;font-size:1.05em;font-weight:600;margin-top:0.85em">4.3 Combine both</h3>

Typical doc pattern:

1. **Mermaid** — IA or flow (where pages connect).
2. **ASCII** — one wireframe per **key screen**.
3. **Table** — routes and labels.

---

<h2 id="tables" style="color:#1565c0;font-size:1.22em;font-weight:650;border-left:4px solid #42a5f5;padding-left:10px;margin-top:1.1em">5. Companion tables</h2>

After each wireframe, add when applicable:

| Nav label | Route | Role / notes |
|---|---|---|
| `{Label}` | `/{path}` | who sees it · shipped vs hold |

Optional third column: content source (doc section, CMS, API) if the design doc maps data.

